WEBVTT

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.820
Anything on the fugitive demons?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.460
I apologize, but there have been
no developments whatsoever.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.450
I see. But it's already been two years...

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.190
I wouldn't be surprised to 
see some major movement soon.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.330
I'm curious about something.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.900
What kind of demon does one turn 
into if not fused with a human?

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.200
They'd be a giant creature 
with no rigidly defined form

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.340
whose body is made out of these tentacles.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.820
Cory-kun seems to have a lot 
of eyes. What about that?

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.470
We all have a lot of eyes,

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:43.860
but most of them look inward after fusing,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.120
so they're hard to confirm.

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:47.730
Pardon me...

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.420
I've actually got a visible one in my mouth.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.490
Not that it serves any purpose—

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.160
Ysley-dono, do you have a moment?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.540
It's got a thin, transparent eyelid, 
like a frog's...

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.290
Could you open a bit wider...?

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.520
Am I interrupting something?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.860
N-No! That's... It's not what 
you're thinking, Barcode.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.050
Sorry. My curiosity got the better of me.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.950
So?

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.150
Well, it turns out...

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.680
So you couldn't control your child
 and have come to us for help?

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.070
I see. The exact kind of major 
movement he was anticipating...

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:32.690
Piscalat! You've got to help him!

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:34.960
How old is he at this point?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.960
Around two months.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:43.080
You'll have to give up, then. Demons can't 
fuse after hitting the two-week mark.

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:48.110
Demons who fail to fuse during that
 two-week period are disposed of, as well.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.310
Did you not know that?

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.340
Oh, no...

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.840
That aside, Buzz, do you know anything 
about the other demons who escaped?

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.510
It's like I already told you.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.490
We didn't discuss our plans.
We just fled in different directions...

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.350
<i>Wait, something's weird here.</i>

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.850
And you don't know anything either, Meliano?

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.100
I don't! I've been with Buzz all this time!

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.110
<i>Piscalat's already suspicious 
of everything I'm saying...</i>

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:17.320
<i>What do I do? Grab Meliano and run?</i>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.660
Looks like we're done with you, in that case.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:27.000
M-Meliano...

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.500
Yeah, I definitely prefer seafood.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.250
You bastard!

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.350
You've gotten a lot more powerful.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.280
You might even be more stronger 
than Nickel was, Cory.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.470
Well, who can say for sure?

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.430
It might've been fun to find out
if Nickel were still alive.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:52.680
So they hid on a deserted island, 
completely isolating themselves...

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.520
I see. A bad choice, though.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.890
Fleeing in a way that you sacrifice
all intel regarding the enemy,

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.610
in exchange for a greater 
sense of security...

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.210
It's the same as when 
people spend their lives

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.970
doing nothing for fear of failure.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.570
The ultimate result...

00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.290
<b>FAILURE</b>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.930
It couldn't be anything <i>but</i> failure.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:24.020
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.000
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:47.970
<b>#10 Demons</b>

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.260
Take that... And that! And that! And that!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.530
You okay, Gill-san?

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.620
I'm fine... I can keep going...

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:17.750
I really don't think so.
Your legs are pointing the wrong way.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.960
Damn, are you two down for the count already?

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.370
This sucks. Granny's still dead on her feet, 
and Prontea doesn't show up anymore...

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.010
You seem kinda bored, Hayato.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.140
Why not fight me?

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:36.200
Who're you again?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.140
<b>Urgh...</b>

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.850
He looks pretty different, 
but I think that's Cory-kun.

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.390
Oh, Cory...

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.530
Come on! Get a grip.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.970
Okay, guess we're doing this.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.780
<i>Cory who, though?</i>

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:55.370
Ysley taught me the best way to use my power!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:58.130
<i>Oh, the kid with the morphing face.</i>

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.890
Now, I'm ready whenever you are!

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.220
Nasty!

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.660
You two! Fight somewhere with more room!

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.710
<i>He's strong! What the hell?</i>

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.340
You wanna take this somewhere else
 since Paula-chan's mad?

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.700
You gotta tell me one thing first.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.750
What training did you do
to get that much stronger so fast?

00:06:56.090 --> 00:07:01.100
Training? I didn't do any. 
I just matured from a kid to an adult.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:07.780
A lion is a whole lot stronger after 
it grows up, right? Same kinda thing.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.280
It's a bit unfair, isn't it?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.620
Being guaranteed extra strength 
just by getting older...

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:17.060
I would think that the Idaten's 
limitless capacity for growth

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.610
via training isn't much fairer.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.340
Do you think Hayato can beat Cory?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.900
Probably not, right?

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:30.380
That said, I could definitely win if I had
 the kind of strength Hayato does.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.910
See, that fleshy armor of 
his has a sense of taste.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.230
So, hypothetically, 
I could spray him head to toe

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.640
with extremely painful hot sauce...

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.270
He'd be unable to focus on fighting.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.850
Alternately, I could do what 
I did when we fought.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.900
P-Please don't remind me!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.000
But Hayato fights won strength alone,
 no strategy or tricks involved.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:55.130
But just like how a trained martial artist

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.660
who's mastered all kinds
of techniques and tactics

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:01.010
pales in comparison to some wild bear...

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.220
There's a kind of extreme combat power 
that only an idiot is capable of mastering.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.520
That's what I want Hayato to achieve.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.070
Mama...

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.060
Okay, here you go.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.470
Now say, "Ah!"

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.080
How are they doing, Merku?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.020
There are no signs of fusion side effects,

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:22.660
and they're growing without trouble so far.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:26.730
Those are your future husbands, 
so make sure you show them lots of love.

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:30.030
I still just can't get behind that...

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.770
Say, Miku, are we seriously going 
to do it with these kids?

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.720
Throw the TV on, would you, Merku?

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:36.780
The TV?

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.740
<i>As you can see, we've got a 
clear shot of the monster!</i>

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:50.030
<i>It's pulling apart this passenger liner
 like it's shelling a crab!</i>

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:47.500
That's...

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.630
Probably either Buzz or Raki. 
One of their kids, anyway.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.540
<i>The ship has been split and two 
and is now falling into the sea.</i>

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:53.260
And this is exactly what I was waiting for.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:56.480
<i>That's quite a splash from the impact...</i>

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:59.010
With demons running amok out in the open, 
the Idaten are bound to focus on them.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.990
This will give us a chance to 
rendezvous with the Demon Lord,

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:04.890
<i>There were an estimated five thousand 
passengers on the ship— Agh!</i>

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.270
and start cooking up some plans!

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.270
Got a package for you.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:08.270
Hey, thanks.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:12.030
A weird robot, a tiny camera, 
and a digital camera...

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:14.280
What's the point of this stuff?

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.280
First, I take a picture of the robot.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.780
Then I update the blog...

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.530
<b>Impulse Purchase~

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:19.980
All done!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:20.530
What?

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.260
It's got speakers that 
can pick up radio waves,

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:25.810
and it's pretty nimble, too...

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:30.220
Once the camera is installed, the Demon Lord 
can use it as a temporary body.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.870
You couldn't do any better than this?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.090
That would've been expensive...

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.620
So, how are you going 
to tell him that blog is ours?

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.050
The internet will do the job 
for me in due time.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:44.430
I anticipated everything up until 
this point when we went on the run.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.940
Which is why the letter I gave His Lordship
 included a way to get in touch.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.270
Wait, really? Then you can just 
call him and let him know.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.660
Not happening.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.690
I'm pretty sure the enemy 
is connected to all telecom in Zoble,

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:01.570
and there's no way to tell what phone number 
he might be using, wherever he is.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.770
Then what did you tell him?

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:06.170
A nonsense phrase.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:10.330
<b>feeling batchyrogeh about it~ (Don't ask what that means*)</b>

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.900
See this part of the blog post?

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.980
What <i>does</i> that mean?

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.110
Nothing at all. I made it up.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:15.990
But that's what makes it special.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:20.570
Because, at present, 
there are no hits for that word.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:21.950
Search

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:24.120
So the first result for it now,

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.310
<b>feeling batchyrogeh</b>

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.310
Your search "feeling batchyrogeh" yielded <b>0 results.</b>

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:29.260
no matter how stupid might seem, 
means it's me!

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:36.850
And as blatant a method as this is,
there's no way to catch on to it.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:41.530
Wait, Miku, once he knows that blog is yours,

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.830
are you just going to post the address here?

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.180
Wouldn't that be dangerous?

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:50.230
What are you talking about, Merku? 
Don't you remember how I found this place?

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:53.590
The information's already out there.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.500
In a way that looks incredibly 
natural, no less.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.200
See? Simple enough, right?

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.100
<i>And she anticipated all of this
starting when we fled?</i>

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.190
<i>That means she knew Zoble would fall,</i>

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.720
<i>that we'd be cut off from communications...</i>

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.100
<i>She knew she'd use
 that internet cafe to plan out</i>

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.190
<i>our lives as shut-ins...</i>

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:15.540
<i>She'd thought this through all the way
 to getting back in touch with the Demon Lord?</i>

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.570
Miku! I can't believe you 
ran off on your own!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.170
Hi! That was faster than I expected.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:23.980
Good to see you again, Your Lordship!

00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.390
Stow the pleasantries, you fool!

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:31.120
<i>She's so many steps ahead,
 it's honestly creepy...</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.150
You must have run a search 
with the perfect timing, sir.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:39.140
Oh, Merku? There was actually 
a set time to do that, you see.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:43.220
The idea was to start searching the 
second there was any major demon activity.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.890
<i>So that was part of the plan, too, huh?</i>

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.100
Things were already afoot, however.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.140
Buzz and Meliano have been taken out.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.570
Huh. So that's their kid, is it?

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:59.030
They were probably begging for help 
with the baby and got killed in the process.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:03.160
Now then, Your Lordship, please tell me 
everything you know about what's going on.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:04.780
Right.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.970
What's with that face, Miku?

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.860
I was just thinking about how boned we are.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:14.590
With Piscalat's crew being brainwashed,

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:19.920
all we've got left is Kuraishi, 
Ferlandia, Kroft, and Raki!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.860
We are thoroughly screwed! 
Can we just give up?

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:25.430
That's extra disheartening 
coming from you, so knock it off!

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:27.810
Right now, I need research facilities.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.860
I can't do a thing in a hovel like this!

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:34.680
I think Kuraishi has got you covered there, 
so why not rendezvous with him?

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.690
And how would I do that?

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:39.170
Can't you do it the same way you found Miku?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:42.680
That only works with a preset password.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.400
Maybe a code, then?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:48.550
The Idaten already have all 
the ciphers we used in Zoble.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:50.930
Any good ideas, Miku?

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:51.990
Sure.

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:52.730
What?!

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.070
He's been calling you periodically, right?

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:57.610
What have you been telling him 
when he does, Your Lordship?

00:12:57.610 --> 00:13:01.900
The names of the surviving demons, 
how Piscalat's group was brainwashed,

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:03.830
the fact that Buzz and his girl are dead...

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:06.660
Oh, how was that going to help at all?

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.180
Give me one second, please.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:11.950
Here. The next time he contacts you,
this is what you'll tell him.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.920
What the hell is this?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.880
<i>Who is it?</i>

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:31.200
<i>You'll want to write this down. 
I'm going to tell you how we'll rendezvous.</i>

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:34.200
<i>This is in a Zoble 3B cipher...</i>

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:34.910
<i>First...</i>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.430
A Zoble 3B cipher?

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.470
It uses a keyword and a password 
in order to put together a message.

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.170
A kind of Caesar shift.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.580
<i>But what exactly is the plan here?</i>

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:48.430
<i>They'll know all of the 
established keywords we use...</i>

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.430
<i>The keyword is...</i>

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:56.180
The password of a video game 
I liked when I was a kid?

00:13:56.510 --> 00:14:00.540
I think it was 
"SoSoSeSoUODhiKoNKoSeChiSaUOToKe."

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.820
What the hell's that mean?

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:06.440
Well, it's sure something 
the Idaten won't figure out.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.780
Damn it!

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.320
Only Miku would cook up such a 
ridiculous means of communication.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:15.660
I don't think using 
a shared memory for a keyword

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:18.670
is that hard for anyone else to come up with.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:22.040
The idea itself is simple enough. However...

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:26.180
Still, how does the His Lordship 
know that password of yours?

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:30.300
What's with your password? 
That part says "Dhik"...

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.080
Hey, just like dick!

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:33.310
What is wrong with you?!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.330
Dick! Dick! Your password has a dick in it!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.560
Quit it, Miku!

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:40.190
It's Miku!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:44.870
I can't believe the stupid 
bitch still remembers that!

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:46.570
So damn creepy!

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.700
Anyway, here's the message.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.700
The Choru train station, Shimau's Toys,
 in the radio section... Okay.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.460
Man, this place is ancient.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:09.420
Radios, radios... Around here?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.500
Hey, Kuraishi.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.460
We've finally managed to connect.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:17.250
Good to see you again, Your Lordship.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.180
Thank you very much!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:26.190
You've met up with Miku's group 
already, right? Where are they?

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.440
I'm apparently not supposed to tell you.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:30.650
Wait, we're not going to rendezvous?

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.750
What would be the point?

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:36.170
It'd just give the Idaten
 a chance to wipe us all out.

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:39.360
Not to mention this whole 
brainwashing thing is scary.

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.790
They'd only need to catch one 
of us to take the rest down.

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.410
That being the case,

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:48.170
the only person who needs to know where 
to find us all is the Demon Lord.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.330
So we're still going through with this, huh?

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.180
Really, Merku? Do you want 
to screw Kuraishi instead?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:54.180
<b>Eep</b>

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.370
In that case, it should be okay if you 
set up a meeting in some forest,

00:15:57.370 --> 00:15:59.490
confirm it's safe, and then breed with him.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:00.400
Breed...

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.310
When you put it that way, 
I'm not so sure anymore.

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:09.320
I've never had natto like this before!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:09.320
Stringy

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:09.320
Stringy

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.190
That'd be helpful since you wouldn't 
have to wait for the boys to grow up...

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.320
But I don't really see it happening.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:12.700
That's what she thinks, anyway. 
What do you say, Kuraishi?

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.600
M-Me and Merku... and Miku?

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:18.480
Look, I don't care if you wanna 
fool around with human chicks,

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:22.030
but if you cheat on me with another 
demon you're dead, asshole!

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:23.830
Right, g-got it...

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:27.350
Oh, Fer-chan, you're so pure of heart!

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.460
Shut the hell up, Miku!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.880
How about a four-way instead, 
then? Does that work?

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:34.230
Is it okay if we're all caught up
 in the heat of the moment?

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:34.840
Drop dead!

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:37.660
Damn, you haven't changed at all, have you?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.600
Well, whatever. We still need to get 
in contact with Raki and Kroft, right?

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.480
Do we, though?

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.480
Kroft is one thing,
 but we don't need Raki, do we?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:49.980
Foremost, she's stupid.

00:16:49.980 --> 00:16:52.930
And considering a single misstep 
could get us all killed,

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:54.510
I think we're better off without her.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:58.140
But if we leave her out there, 
she might actually come in handy.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:16:59.990
Oh, it moved.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.580
I'm back, Raki. How are you...

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:10.060
You lost a lot of weight while 
I was out hunting, I see.

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:10.840
Where's the child?

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.780
Just had it.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:15.470
So into the ocean it goes.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.970
Well, they're just monsters, after all.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:21.970
Forget about that. Come on, Kroft...

00:17:37.880 --> 00:17:40.580
<b>Seven years later</b>

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.160
Oh... a whale...

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:55.880
Haven't seen one of those around 
here in a hundred years...

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.760
But it got eaten, huh?

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.650
<i>It's gone already. Must have escaped.</i>

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.620
<i>A demon... Was that a demon?</i>

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:32.040
Ow, ow, ow... I surrender! I surrender!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:34.710
Hell, yeah!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.990
All right! We win again!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:40.890
We can beat him pretty consistently 
now! He's not so tough!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:40.890
<i>All of a sudden, Gill-san is 
able to keep up with Hayato?!</i>

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:43.640
Gill-san's been growing at an abnormal rate.

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:48.690
I'd wager the large amount of humanoid demon 
thoughts contributed to her manifestation...

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.860
Which is all fine and dandy, 
but here's our big problem.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.570
This definitely isn't good.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:00.950
It's the fourth one, too.

00:19:00.950 --> 00:19:04.780
It's safe to assume that pure-blooded 
demons are starting to mate.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:06.300
It's strange, though.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:11.130
From what Master and Piscalat told us, 
they shouldn't be reproducing this quickly.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:14.790
With humanoid demons, we've got a good idea 
of how their reproductive cycles work.

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.920
They often abort cases that fail the fusion...

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:21.170
So the real reason I think the 
pure-blooded demon population

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.800
is exploding is because of their diet.

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.800
In the old days, demons starving to death

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:27.310
and cannibalizing each other 
was a regular occurrence...

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:30.760
But now, there's life in essentially 
every corner of the planet.

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:32.870
We shouldn't assume the pattern sticks

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:34.920
with a much larger food supply around.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.000
I see...

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.690
This has turned into a real mess.

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:41.040
And the wanted posters?

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:45.370
All we're getting is bad tips that sound fake...

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:47.830
To be honest, they may have 
had the opposite effect.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.290
<b>Hey! Miku!!

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.040
Huh, so we're fugitives now?

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.550
<b>National Wanted List</b>

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.550
<b>Miku                     Umeyo              Kuraishi           Ferlandia</b>

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.020
What a waste of effort!

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:01.420
I wonder what the big rush is.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:04.800
Miku-neechan, I'm back. I brought food.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.460
Welcome home, Teta-kun!

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:08.480
What now? Do you want to eat?

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:10.350
Or would you rather play first?

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.810
U-Um... I wanna play first.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.180
You're such a needy boy, aren't you?

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:19.820
Do you want to play with me
 or Merku-oneechan today?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.820
This lifestyle is so debauched...

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:24.070
A little <i>too</i> debauched!

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.160
Nah.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.830
I'm honestly disgusted with 
how much I'm enjoying it.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:34.640
H-Hey, isn't she that fugitive?

00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:36.410
The one worth 100 mill?!

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.710
Hurry and take a shot!

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:40.710
Make sure you get my good side, okay?

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.250
Hello?! Hello?!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.390
Yes, it's the that fugitive on the poster!

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:44.470
Right, she's on walking 
down the street in Central!

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:44.470
How does the reward get split now?!

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:46.360
Miku's on Central Road!

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:47.070
Reports are flooding in!

00:20:47.070 --> 00:20:48.540
I want that video here! Now!

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:51.980
<i>Come on, you can get a closer shot than that!</i>

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:53.920
Is this really her?

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:57.680
Yes. That voice and appearance
 are definitely Miku's.

00:20:57.680 --> 00:21:00.230
But what is she after?

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:06.110
Screw this! If I just catch her myself, 
that means I get the whole reward!

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:10.080
Sorry, but no touching.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.390
R-Run for it!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.630
Okay, I should probably clear out.
